{"id": "EUVD-2026-107896", "enisaUuid": "f57bad67-9c00-3e8d-bc27-bbf8cbce43ba", "description": "Traefik 2.11.x before 2.11.58 and 3.x before 3.7.14 contains a race condition in NTLM and Kerberos (Negotiate) backend authentication, where the per-connection sticky round tripper slot is read and written without synchronization. Remote attackers can send concurrent HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 requests over one connection to orphan backend connections, break connection-bound authentication, or crash Traefik.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:43:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:43:40", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/traefik/traefik/security/advisories/GHSA-mhjw-hmjv-p99x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/traefik-before-2.11.58-and-3.7.14-race-condition-in-ntlm-kerberos-round-tripper"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114641", "GHSA-q9pf-jh7g-83mc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "65c5b222-68f6-355b-81ce-93a5bf43ebec", "product": {"name": "traefik", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.7.14"}, {"id": "6918af36-9bc0-3045-b757-b4b16cf24be5", "product": {"name": "traefik", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}, "product_version": "2.11.0 <2.11.58"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b11c17b-725c-3114-9d56-3c1ed44f44f2", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}], "isExploited": false}